     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914397,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N1CCNCC1"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=[N+]([O-])c1cc(Br)c2c(c1)CCC1(CCC1)O2"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Now the second precursor of that reaction (the brominated nitro aromatic) will have reaction 1914398.

So that aromatic nitro bromide mol object with children reaction 1914398.

{
